Flang's runtime type builder must model the Windows 64-bit memory-copy callback
signature for both the MSVC and GNU Windows targets. MinGW uses the same
64-bit size argument but does not define _MSC_VER, leaving getModel undefined
when ThinLTO links the Flang driver.

diff --git a/flang/include/flang/Optimizer/Builder/Runtime/RTBuilder.h b/flang/include/flang/Optimizer/Builder/Runtime/RTBuilder.h
--- a/flang/include/flang/Optimizer/Builder/Runtime/RTBuilder.h
+++ b/flang/include/flang/Optimizer/Builder/Runtime/RTBuilder.h
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ getModel<void *(*)(void *, const void *, unsigned long)>() {
   };
 }
-#ifdef _MSC_VER
+#ifdef _WIN32
 template <>
 constexpr TypeBuilderFunc
 getModel<void *(*)(void *, const void *, unsigned __int64)>() {
